[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="ferdnyc"
 avatar="http://cdn.libravatar.org/avatar/0a1d7aeb5a21edb0fcce12df464ff13b"
 subject="There is no difference"
 date="2026-06-16T15:04:33Z"
 content="""
If you look at `/etc/etckeeper/vcs.d/50vcs-cmd` (which is the script that receives the arguments to `etckeeper vcs`),
all it does is run,

```
$VCS \"$@\"
```

So it passes the commands right through to `git`.

The only reason to use `etckeeper vcs ...` is if you're writing generic scripts that can't assume a particular underlying VCS. (And even then, since most of them have different syntax anything but the most basic commands won't be portable.)
"""]]
